  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14689762",
      "title": "Using Different \"in\" and \"out\" Transitions",
      "lectureOrder": 133,
      "videoOrder": 117,
      "sourceHash": "dffba82c89e3ffbfe2818026ecad378a864d011857f2922df96678b6f98dd52b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 8.22,
          "en": "Maybe you also have different animations for adding and removing an element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 8.61,
          "end": 13.86,
          "en": "So maybe you want to fly the element in when you add it, but when it's removed from the Dom, it should",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 15.24,
          "en": "just fade out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 15.27,
          "end": 18.69,
          "en": "That's also something you can easily implement with svelte.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 18.72,
          "end": 21.12,
          "en": "For that, let me go back to this paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21.88,
          "end": 28.1,
          "en": "Let's say upon adding this element, I indeed want to just fade it in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 28.12,
          "end": 32.35,
          "en": "Then you can do this by using the in directive instead of transition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 32.35,
          "end": 37.39,
          "en": "And then the name of the animation you want to use, for example, fade.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 37.66,
          "end": 42.04,
          "en": "Now for removing it, I want to use fly and therefore you can use out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 42.1,
          "end": 47.53,
          "en": "Now one important difference to transition is not just that you now have two different kinds of transitions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 47.53,
          "end": 52.9,
          "en": "but that now you can't cancel them in between because they are different animations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 52.9,
          "end": 53.35,
          "en": "Right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 53.35,
          "end": 56.77,
          "en": "And even if you had the same one here, Svelte wouldn't know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 56.77,
          "end": 62.83,
          "en": "So in and out are not cancelable they don't have this effect which transition has where you can cancel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 62.83,
          "end": 67.69,
          "en": "it in between and it smoothly plays back the animation that is not available here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 67.87,
          "end": 70.63,
          "en": "But the upside is that we now have two different animations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 70.63,
          "end": 74.32,
          "en": "So if I click toggle here, watch the paragraph, you see it, fade it in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 74.32,
          "end": 76.8,
          "en": "But if I click toggle again, it flies out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 76.84,
          "end": 79.69,
          "en": "Now if I hit this real quick, you see, that is what I meant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 79.69,
          "end": 82.4,
          "en": "It does not play this back because it can't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 83.6,
          "end": 84.92,
          "en": "So in and out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 84.92,
          "end": 88.07,
          "en": "Also really useful to achieve the look you want.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
